course: dictionary
lesson: 15726
title: Transcribed: writing it down, copying it over
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To transcribe something means to write it down carefully, copying it word for word or moving it into another form. «Ravi transcribed the interview for his school project.» He listened to the recording and wrote down every word.
explain: Transcribed is the past tense of transcribe, so it tells you the job is already done. The same word changes its ending for time: transcribe, transcribes, transcribed, transcribing. «The old letter was transcribed so everyone could read it.»
explain: Use the clues around the word. If something is recorded, handwritten or written in one form and then copied into another, it has probably been transcribed. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "wrote it down carefully" make sense there? Then it is right.
fact: Transcribed is the past tense of transcribe.
fact: «Transcribed» can mean wrote down exactly what someone said, or what was recorded.
fact: «Transcribed» can also mean copied writing from one form to another, such as from handwriting into typing.
fact: In music, a song can be transcribed, which means it is changed so it can be played on a different instrument.
fact: Words can be transcribed using special symbols that show their sounds, which is called phonetic writing.
exercise: «Mia transcribed the interview word for word.» What does transcribed mean here? | *Wrote down exactly what was said | Lost the recording | Painted a picture of the room
exercise: «Dad transcribed the handwritten recipe into a document on the computer.» What did Dad do? | *Copied it from handwriting into typing | Threw the recipe away | Read it out loud to the dog
exercise: «The song was transcribed so it could be played on the piano.» What was changed? | The song was made shorter for the radio | *The music was changed so it could be played on a different instrument | The piano was painted a new colour
test: Which word is the past tense of transcribe? | transcribes | *transcribed | transcribing | transcribe
test: «The scientist transcribed the sounds using special symbols.» What does transcribed mean here? | Cooked a meal | Ran quickly to the door | *Wrote down using symbols that show sounds | Drew a map of the lab
exam: «The notes from the meeting were transcribed into a neat booklet.» What does transcribed most likely mean? | *Copied from one form into another | Scribbled in the margins | Hid under the table | Shouted at
